                label: 'Personal and home care brands',
                text: "**Jyothy Labs** (Ujala, Henko, Exo, Maxo, Margo) makes detergents, dishwash, mosquito repellents and soap in its own cheap plants; about 90% of its business uses crude-linked chemicals such as LABSA and plastic packaging, so its margin swings with crude. **Honasa** (Mamaearth, The Derma Co) owns no factories: contract makers produce its creams and shampoos, and it spends about a third of revenue on advertising and influencers instead. **Bajaj Consumer Care** bottles hair oil, mainly Almond Drops, a light oil made on liquid paraffin with almond and other oils, in its own plants and sells it in small packs and sachets through lakhs of village and town shops; its inputs are paraffin, edible oils and plastic. **For all three, the fight is for shelf space and search rank**, and prices are set by what Hindustan Unilever, Marico and other giants charge.",
