        salesDrivers: ["**US and European car programmes**: exports to car makers rose from ₹194cr to ₹290cr in FY26, and management expects its US car business to grow 60–70% over three years from existing customers (Ford, Chrysler). Guidance is 10–15% overall revenue growth a year for three years.", "**Indian car production and the replacement market**: steady rather than fast; in August management said it was not looking for very strong growth at home, with the growth to come from exports (in May it had guided 8–10% domestic value growth).", "**Footwear demand**, which is weak: shoe makers cut orders as PVC and sole prices rose two to three times in 2026.", "**Capacity**: PVC lines run at 75–78%. A ₹50cr line in the existing Jaipur plant, due February–March 2027, adds about 15% (5 lakh metres a month) and can bring ₹120–150cr of sales at about ₹300 a metre, roughly three rupees of sales per rupee spent. A ₹250–300cr plant near North American car makers is on hold because of US tariffs and the war.", "**The rupee**: export prices are in dollars, so a weaker rupee lifts margins; a currency gain of about ₹30cr in FY26 flattered profit."],
