        costEffect: "**Mostly passed on, through pack sizes more than prices.** The company cut the ml in key packs in Q3–Q4 FY26 and took selective price rises in Q1 FY27; it buys ahead, which covered ‘a good portion’ of the quarter when prices spiked. **Rule of thumb:** a 10% rise in material costs not passed on would cut the margin by about 4 points (19% to 15%). **What happened:** there is no price index in the chart. The margin slid from about 30% in FY19 to 13% in FY25 as costs rose and sales stalled; smaller packs, price and discount changes in coconut oil, mix and cost savings lifted it to 19% in FY26 (despite dear copra) and 24% in Q1 FY27, even as paraffin, packaging and edible oils rose again after the West Asia war. Q2 gross margin fell to 59.9% (60.8% for H1), but lower fixed and staff costs held the operating margin at 25%; it will take about 5% more from consumers in Q3, half by price and half through smaller packs.",
